{
  "id": "reverse_bits",
  "fn": "reverse_bits",
  "in": 2,
  "out": 1,
  "desc": "Given (n, w), reverse the low w bits of n and return the result as a non-negative integer. w is in [1,63]. Only the low w bits of n participate: bit i (for i in [0,w-1]) of n becomes bit (w-1-i) of the result; all bits of n at position >= w are IGNORED (not just zeroed afterward — they must never leak into the answer). n may be negative; use its low w two's-complement bits (extract each bit with a logical right shift then mask with 1). Examples: reverse_bits(178,8): 178=0b10110010 reverses to 0b01001101=77. reverse_bits(1,8)=128 (bit0 -> bit7). reverse_bits(1,1)=1. reverse_bits(-1,8)=255 (low 8 bits all 1). reverse_bits(1,63)=2^62. Output is in [0, 2^w - 1].",
